:: Millers Babysitting Isaiah Video Games [nobr]

/* Intro */

You sit down on <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span>’s couch, sinking into the cushions as you grab his controller and load up his console. <span style="Color: LightGreen">You feel a bit jealous that <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span> gets to have not only a couch and TV in his bedroom, but also a full console that he doesn’t seem to have to share with his brothers! Some kids get all the luck.</span> Oh well, at least you can use this time to unwind and relax, you doubt he’d mind you playing a few rounds on his games. <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Smirk",
                Eyes: "Mad",
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<<set _random to random(1, 4)>>
<<if _random == 1>>
    His game console hums to life, and the screen lights up to a space-themed shooter. The menu shows a save file labeled <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Zay’s Campaign”</span>. You smile to yourself, though decide it would be best not to mess with his save files, <span style="Color: Yellow">for that is a line no one should ever cross,</span> and instead load up a new game on an empty save file. <br>
    <br>
    As you pilot a spaceship through asteroid fields and enemy fleets, the screen fills with explosions. Laser blasts and booming sound effects echo in the room as you weave through the chaos. He didn’t seem to have any headphones for his game and you are a bit worried you may alert <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> to what you are doing, but figure the sound must not travel well in this house, which makes sense in a house full of people into music. So, you just sit back and enjoy the sounds as you weave through the chaos, narrowly dodging enemy fire. <br>
    <br>
    After you beat the first few levels, you decide to call it quits and stretch your arms into the air. While you don’t think <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span> would care, you make sure to delete your save file, just to ensure your friend had no idea you were here. <span style="Color: LightGreen">Mainly for your own satisfaction of doing something without his knowledge.</span> <br>
    <<needChange "Fun" 8>>
    <br>
    [[Continue|OC Miller House Isaiah Room]]

<<elseif _random == 2>>
    You spend a few minutes scrolling through <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span>’s game library before landing on a sports game. Loading it up, you settle deeper into the couch for a relaxing match. The menu shows <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span>’s profile with a team decked out in custom colors – black and gray. You start a match and select a rival team to face off against <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span>’s, imagining you were versing the boy himself. <br>
    <br>
    The game is face-paced, and every goal or point sends a surge of adrenaline through you, slowly bringing you from buried deep in the couch to the very edge. You pull off a perfectly timed combo at one point, scoring a goal that makes you laugh out loud. When victory finally displays on the screen, you managing to win by just a single point, you cheer and celebrate. <span style="Color: LightGreen">You wonder if that match will stay on record and wonder what <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span> will think if he discovers his favorite team had lost a match to their rivals on his very own console.</span> <br>
    <<needChange "Fun" 8>>
    <br>
    [[Continue|OC Miller House Isaiah Room]]

<<elseif _random == 3>>
    While browsing through <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span>’s console, you come across a puzzle game that looks oddly relaxing. The screen fills with vibrant colors and soothing music as you arrange blocks to solve increasingly challenging puzzles. You get so lost in the gameplay, trying to outscore the leaderboard record, that you lose track of time. At the top of the charts is the name <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“ZayTheGreat”</span>. Smirking, you focus harder, determined to beat his high score just as a way to tease the boy in the future without him knowing. <br>
    <br>
    After a few challenging attempts, you eventually finish with the flashing words <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“New High Score!”</span> blinking in the center of the screen. <span style="Color: LightGreen">You smile as you enter in a teasing name, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“ZayTheBaby”</span> before closing the game and leaning back on the couch, satisfied and wondering how your friend will react when he discovers it.</span> <br>
    <<needChange "Fun" 8>>
    <br>
    [[Continue|OC Miller House Isaiah Room]]

<<elseif _random == 4>>
    Curious about <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span>’s taste in gaming, you find yourself looking in the titles buried deep in his library, before eventually selecting an adventure game with mysterious forests and secret caves. You settle into the couch, gripping the controller as the story unfolds. The game is surprisingly immersive, with your character sneaking through shadowy ruins and solving riddles that really wrack your brain as the environment keeps you on edge. <br>
    <br>
    You manage to unlock a hidden treasure at one point, the screen flashing <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Rare Item Unlocked”</span> as you explore deeper and deeper into the game’s world. The comforting hum of the console and the glow on the screen makes you lose track of time. Eventually, you call it quits and sadly delete your save file to remove any trace that you were playing it. <span style="Color: LightGreen">Still, that game was pretty fun!</span> <br>
    <<needChange "Fun" 8>>
    <br>
    [[Continue|OC Miller House Isaiah Room]]

<</if>>